WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.869 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hello and welcome to playstation grenade  there is a huge update coming to ps plus  this november and i think we should look  at it  in a little more detail to coincide with  the release of the ps5  there will be 18 games free to play  right away  you heard me right 18. i thought we  should quickly break them down so you  know once and for all if you're going to  make the jump to ps5  right away or wait a little while here's  every game so far revealed in the ps  plus collection dropping on november  12th  let's start with the games that have  never appeared on ps plus before and the  biggest game on the list  is god of war the 2018 game of the year  which in many people's eyes is the game  of the generation  playing as kratos as he leads greek  mythology behind to venture into the  lands of odin  and thor and norse mythology a blend of  hack and slash action  reaction based combat and puzzle solving  along the way  but the story is another huge selling  point as we discover secrets about the  god of war and his family  this game has so many 10 out of 10  review scores it will blow your puny  mind  another playstation exclusive is days  gone a zombie apocalypse game in which  cannibalistic freakers are trying to eat  you alive  playing as deacon we survive the  outbreak and move freely around the open  world  thanks to our motorcycle due to many  patches and updates the game is in a far  better place than it was when released  in 2019  and come november it's all yours persona  5 is yet another exclusive title on ps4  this is a role-playing game following  the schedule of a tokyo high school  over the year we discover some special  powers  persona games can be a bit daunting at  first as there is an element of dungeon  crawling digital novels and  even sim-like social scenarios so maybe  if you're still thinking this isn't the  game for you when november arrives you  can try it without putting your money on  the line  you'll be surprised how great this  series is back in 2001  and 2005 two brilliant games released  these were ico  and shadow of the colossus there was a  third game planned but it didn't see the  light of day until  2016 and finished that trilogy  the last guardian has never appeared on  ps plus before but in november  it will so if you've ever wanted to play  as a young boy with a half bird dog  thing following you around  your prayers are answered there are more  playstation exclusives and timed  exclusives but we  had them on ps plus before so i'll  quickly go over them now  let's do the third person action  adventure style games first the last of  us remastered  once again stays attached to ps plus and  the journey of ellie and joel through  zombified america  uncharted 4 a thief's end finishes up  the nathan drake storyline in epic  fashion  infamous second son was on ps plus back  in 2017  and gave us super powers and an open  world with a morality system which lets  us be good  or downright evil i know which one you  chose  the ps4 exclusives keep on coming  bloodborne returns to ps plus in  november which is everything  but another game in the soul series you  know the drill these games are  punishment  as you slowly venture forward you will  die time and time again  these games are for the hardcore purists  which is why  five years later i still haven't  finished it wait there's more exclusive  games until dawn will return to ps plus  as we play through an interactive horror  story perfect for the kids  no it's certainly most not perfect for  the kids it is filled with anxiety and  jump scares  it's great if platforming is your jam  then note that ratchet and clank are  coming back to ps plus too  a perfect chance to be reacquainted  before the new rift apart sequel drops  and the last playstation console  exclusive is the return of detroit  become  human taking control of many synthetic  humans as we choose our own adventure  to fight oppression or to run and hide  this is the game with multiple paths and  endings  with tons of replayability we still have  seven more games to go through  six of them are brand new to ps plus  let's start with horror  resident evil 7 biohazard takes the  third person game and shoves it in first  person  as we take on a new protagonist to find  his lost wife  this game is filled with poop your pants  moments especially in the first three  hours  and it's psvr compatible too which  honestly  is the scariest thing i've ever played  in my life if you prefer to brawl and  check out mortal kombat x  notice that this isn't the latest game  in the series but still  a highly accomplished fighter with  stylized brutal action throughout  a great game to settle disputes at home  what about cooperative hunting  if you have never played a monster  hunter game before try monster hunter  world  you and three other buddies prepare to  track down take down  or capture a legendary animal we then  use their body parts to create  new armor sets and weapons allowing the  squad to take on the next tier of hunt  it's crazy addictive with the right  people and with regular crossover events  like  ryu from street fighter popping up there  is content for months  there's an online first person shooter  included in the collection 2  battlefield 1 the world war 1 outing  from 2016  packed with tons of game modes but i  have to be honest not many people play  this one online these days  it was released in 2016 remember but the  campaign is still  eye-opening remember when fallout games  were great yeah me too  which brings me to fallout 4. another  open world apocalypse filled with toxic  creatures and tentative alliances  fallout 4 is a classic of our time let's  not let fallout 76 ruin this moment  and we can't have a ps plus collection  without a final fantasy game can we  well this time it's final fantasy xv  released in 2016.  this iteration of the franchise includes  the real-time battle system which makes  every encounter more impactful than the  previous turn-based combat  other than that this is the role-playing  game you know the franchise for  and this time there's a flying car too  and finally if anyone is still here the  last game is batman arkham  knight the final part of the arkham  series although we now know this  timeline is continued in the upcoming  suicide squad game  so right now is a good time to look for  references  to that game's continuity using batman's  detective vision  and the utterly brilliant arkham  fighting system too  so there we have it 18 games completely  free coming to ps plus  in november it looks like there's  something for everyone and many  returning games that people loved in the  past  i'd love to know your thoughts and if  you've stayed this long hit me with a  dad joke please  i'll be watching i'm adam from  playstation grenade it's been a pleasure  see you next time

